    {
      "title": "Karthigai Deepam row: SC issues contempt notice to Tamil Nadu officials",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/karthigai-deepam-row-sc-issues-contempt-notice-to-tamil-nadu-officials-126112700725_1.html",
      "description": "Observing that the executive authorities in Tamil Nadu acted on the diktat of their political bosses, the Supreme Court on Friday issued a contempt notice to the Tamil Nadu chief secretary, DGP, Madurai collector and others over the violation of its November 20 Karthigai Deepam order.\nThe top court suspended the board of trustees of Arulmigu Subramaniaswamy temple and ordered lighting of lamp at Thiruparankundram Deepathoon on Saturday using the flame lit at Uchaipillaiyar mandapam.\nAsking the Tamil Nadu chief secretary to appear personally, a bench of Justices Aravind Kumar and Vipul M Pancholi directed him to file an affidavit detailing emails, calls exchanged and messages exchanged between officials.\n\"The wilful non-compliance of orders of the Court, especially by the executive authorities, cannot go unnoticed and it has to be dealt with an iron hand,\" the bench said.\nThe top court also handed over the security of Tamil Nadu's Arulmigu Subramaniaswamy temple and Thiruparankundra",
